.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="G. N. Lewis replaced pressure by the fugacity f = \phi P so that the ideal-gas form \mu = \mu^\circ + RT\ln(f/P^\circ) stays exact for real fluids. The left panel shows the fugacity coefficient \phi of supercritical CO2 computed by fugacity_coefficient from three equations of state. The right panel shows Lewis&#x27;s phase-equilibrium criterion: below T_c the liquid and vapor fugacities from fugacity cross exactly at the saturation pressure.">

